  "decisionGap": "The guide still tells readers the 2027 Part B premium has not been announced (or cites the $209.50 Trustees projection), although CMS announced the final figure on November 17, 2026.",
  "finding": "CMS set the 2027 standard Medicare Part B premium at $209.40, up $6.50 from $202.90 in 2026, with a $292 annual deductible (up $9 from $283). On a $2,000 benefit the 3.6% COLA adds $72, so the net monthly gain after the premium increase is $65.50.",
